_meanings:
A teacher, preceptor, instructor especially
 of the Vedas; {#vyAkaraRa˚, nyAya˚#} professor or teacher of grammar,
 logic <ab>&c.</ab>; {#Bftaka˚#} a hired teacher, mercenary teacher; {#˚uditaH#}
 styled a professor. According to Viṣṇu-Smṛti an {%adhyāpaka%} is of 2
 kinds: he is either an {%Achārya%} <ab>i. e.</ab> one who invests a boy with
 the sacred thread and initiates him into the Vedas, or he is an {%Upādhyāya%}
 <ab>i. e.</ab> one who teaches for livelihood ({#vfttyarTam#}) See <ls>Ms. 2. 140-141</ls>.
 and the two words. [{#upanIya tu yaH SizyaM vedamaDyApayeddvijaH . sakalpaM#}
